---
/**
 * Pie — canonical footer of every page (design-system.md §7, item 16 "Pie
 * (`Pie`)"; reference implementation at
 * design/ds/components/navegacion/Pie.jsx; approved markup in the `<footer>`
 * of every `design/*.dc.html`, identical in all 25 screens). It is the same on
 * the nine pages of the approved design and has no variants
 * (diseno-web-indice.md, decision 2: "el Pie es único en todo el sitio y no
 * tiene variantes"; it keeps its `FranjaAliados` even on a page that already
 * has an "Aliados" section).
 *
 * Fixed order, per §7.16 and decision 2: `FranjaAliados` (SM-023) →
 * `HiloTricolor` (SM-024) → `Sello` (SM-017) → mono contact block →
 * "¡Aguante la fotografía!" as an `Anotacion` (SM-018). The block is never
 * omitted when data is missing: the contact values fall back to the visible
 * placeholders of `.env.example` (CLAUDE.md, "No inventar datos").
 *
 * Geometry read off the láminas (all 25 `<footer>` elements carry the same
 * inline style, so this is the spec, not one screen's accident):
 * `flex-direction: column`, `gap: 32px` (`gap-8`), `padding: 48px 48px 32px`
 * desktop / `40px 24px 24px` mobile, and `border-top: 1px solid #D9D6CF` —
 * the `linea` token at 1px, the same border `Nav.astro`'s `<header>` uses on
 * its other edge, NOT the 2px `tinta` rule the SM-012 skeleton carried.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (layout width): unlike every `<section>` of the láminas, the
 * `<footer>` has no `max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto` — it is full-bleed
 * with only its own 48/24px side padding, so at 1440 the footer's contents are
 * wider than the 1280px container above them. Consistent across all 25
 * screens, so it is reproduced as approved (`px-6 md:px-12`, no
 * `.contenedor`), which is also what SM-027 did with the `<header>`. Flagged
 * because diseno-web-indice.md's "Constantes de layout" describes the site as
 * a 1280px container and does not mention this exception.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (footer background): the láminas give the `<footer>` no
 * background of its own, so the paper grain and specks of `body.papel` show
 * through it. The SM-012 skeleton painted it `bg-papel-puro` (opaque white),
 * which both hid the grain and put a white band under a `#FBFAF7` page.
 * Removed here to match the design; `Nav.astro`'s `bg-papel` is a different
 * case (an opaque bar the mobile menu slides under).
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (handwritten size): the láminas set the closing annotation at
 * `2.25rem` desktop / `1.75rem` mobile, and the reference
 * `design/ds/components/expediente/Anotacion.jsx` does expose the prop they
 * use for it (`tamano = "var(--tipo-manuscrita)"`, which `Pie.jsx` overrides
 * with `clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem)`). `Anotacion.astro` (SM-018) has no such
 * prop and renders the fixed `text-manuscrita` token of design-system.md §4,
 * `clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem)` — 1.5rem at 390 and 3rem at 1440, so the closing
 * line is larger than the lámina's at desktop width. That is the only visible
 * difference between this footer and the approved screen, and it also shifts
 * the second contact column ~50px left, since a wider annotation leaves the
 * `flex-1` contact grid less room. Not fixed here: adding a prop to another
 * ticket's canonical component is outside this ticket's scope, and the
 * skeleton's workaround — a raw `<span class="font-manuscrita">` instead of
 * the canonical `Anotacion` — contradicts §7.16 and decision 2.
 * Ruben/SM-018 to decide whether `Anotacion` gains `tamano` or whether §4's
 * token wins over the láminas.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (global link rule): the design system ships a base rule
 * (`design/_ds/…/tokens/texturas.css`: `a { color: azul-sello;
 * text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; transition: color
 * var(--duracion-rapida) ease }`, plus `a:hover` azul-marcador and `a:active`
 * azul-profundo) that `src/styles/` does not carry, while Tailwind's preflight
 * resets `text-decoration` to `inherit` — so a link in this project renders
 * bare unless its component says otherwise, and the footer's underlined
 * handle would have been lost. Applied per-element on the Instagram link
 * below, which is what the lámina shows, rather than added globally: a global
 * `a` rule would silently restyle every other component's links,
 * `Nav.astro`'s and `Boton.astro`'s among them. Worth deciding site-wide
 * outside this ticket.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (unconfirmed partners, question handed here by
 * `FranjaAliados.astro`): this ticket's criterion is "los aliados sin confirmar
 * no muestran nombre", and that holds — the strip renders no caption at all,
 * and `FranjaAliados` drops the `aria-label` for an aliado with
 * `confirmado: false`, so the two unconfirmed logos are announced by their
 * generic `logoAlt` ("Logo tricolor de manos", "Logo de CCC") and never by the
 * `[NOMBRE ALIADO LOGO TRICOLOR DE MANOS]` placeholder. They do stay LINKED,
 * to their real Instagram handles (`@redvoluntariosba`, `@creercrearcompartir`)
 * and never to their `[URL …]` placeholders, which honours "nunca un href que
 * sea un placeholder". The láminas' `renderVals()` omit `href` for those two
 * altogether, while modelo-de-contenido.md §5 ties `confirmado` only to the
 * name: `FranjaAliados` follows the prose and this footer does not override it
 * (the alternative would mean editing another ticket's component to add a
 * behaviour Ruben has not decided). Ruben to confirm on purpose whether an
 * unconfirmed partner keeps its link.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (`pie.aliados`): the dictionaries carry
 * `pie.aliados` = `[ALIADOS]` / `[PARTNERS]` as a possible label for the
 * strip. No lámina shows any heading over the logos, so none is rendered and
 * the key is left unused rather than invented into the design
 * (`FranjaAliados.astro` explicitly hands this decision to this ticket).
 */
import { getCollection, type CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

import Anotacion from './Anotacion.astro';
import FranjaAliados from './FranjaAliados.astro';
import HiloTricolor from './HiloTricolor.astro';
import Sello from './Sello.astro';
import selloCompacto from '../assets/marca/sello-compacto.png';
import { type Idioma, t } from '../i18n/utils.ts';

interface Props {
  idioma: Idioma;
  /**
   * Partner strip override, in render order. Defaults to the whole `aliados`
   * collection ordered as the approved design shows it (see `ordenarAliados`).
   * Part of this component's prop contract in PLAN.md §5 and kept for a caller
   * that needs to narrow or reorder the strip; no page passes it today, since
   * the footer is identical site-wide (diseno-web-indice.md, decision 2).
   */
  aliados?: CollectionEntry<'aliados'>[];
}

const { idioma, aliados: aliadosProp } = Astro.props;

/**
 * `getCollection('aliados')` yields entries sorted by id (ccc, consulado,
 * infiltrado, manos-tricolor), which is not the approved order: every lámina's
 * `renderVals()` lists CONSULADO · manos tricolor · infiltrado™ · CCC, which
 * is exactly the `aliados` array of `src/content/ediciones/buenos-aires-2026.md`.
 * So the edition's reference list is the source of order, and any aliado it
 * does not mention follows, by id, so a partner added to the collection never
 * silently disappears from the footer.
 */
function ordenarAliados(
  todos: CollectionEntry<'aliados'>[],
  orden: string[]
): CollectionEntry<'aliados'>[] {
  const posicion = new Map(orden.map((id, indice) => [id, indice]));
  return [...todos].sort((a, b) => {
    const posicionA = posicion.get(a.id) ?? Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
    const posicionB = posicion.get(b.id) ?? Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
    if (posicionA !== posicionB) return posicionA - posicionB;
    return a.id.localeCompare(b.id);
  });
}

/**
 * The footer stamp is the real scan `marca/sello-compacto.png`, which reads
 * "SERES MIGRATORIOS / BUENOS AIRES / 08 AGO 2026" — edition 01's stamp. Its
 * `ciudad`/`fecha` props feed `Sello`'s `alt`, so they must describe THAT
 * image and not the newest edition: the oldest edition by `fecha` (edition 01)
 * is the one the scan depicts. A future edition with its own compact scan
 * changes the asset and this lookup together.
 */
const ediciones = await getCollection('ediciones');
const edicionMasAntigua = [...ediciones].sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.fecha.getTime() - b.data.fecha.getTime()
)[0];

const aliados =
  aliadosProp ??
  ordenarAliados(
    await getCollection('aliados'),
    edicionMasAntigua?.data.aliados.map((referencia) => referencia.id) ?? []
  );

// A site with no edition in the collection cannot happen today (the loader
// requires at least the seed edition), but the stamp still needs two strings:
// the bilingual "[A CONFIRMAR]" placeholder rather than an invented city.
const aConfirmar = t(idioma, 'estados.aConfirmar');
const selloCiudad = edicionMasAntigua?.data.sello.ciudad ?? aConfirmar;
const selloFecha = edicionMasAntigua?.data.sello.fechaCorta ?? aConfirmar;

/**
 * A `PUBLIC_*` variable of PLAN.md §14 as a string. Vite types `import.meta.env`
 * with an `any` index signature, so the value is narrowed here instead of
 * spreading `any` through the component. An empty value falls back too, the way
 * astro.config.mjs treats `PUBLIC_SITE_URL`.
 */
function variablePublica(valor: unknown, respaldo: string): string {
  return typeof valor === 'string' && valor !== '' ? valor : respaldo;
}

// The collective has no address yet: the fallback is the visible placeholder of
// .env.example, and the value is plain text rather than a `mailto:` so an
// unresolved placeholder never becomes a broken link. The láminas render it as
// plain text too, never as a link.
const email = variablePublica(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_EMAIL_CONTACTO, '[EMAIL DEL COLECTIVO]');

// Unlike the email, PLAN.md §14 and .env.example carry the real Instagram URL,
// so the fallback is that value and not a placeholder.
const instagram = variablePublica(
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_URL,
  'https://www.instagram.com/seresmigratorios/'
);

/** Official handle (design system §13, v1.1). A handle is never translated. */
const HANDLE = '@seresmigratorios';
---

<footer class="border-t border-linea flex flex-col gap-8 px-6 pt-10 pb-6 md:px-12 md:pt-12 md:pb-8">
  {
    /* Defaults are exactly the footer's spec — 36px/40px centered on desktop,
      28px/24px left-aligned below it — so no size prop is passed here; see the
      "Two approved uses" note in FranjaAliados.astro. Skipped entirely with an
      empty collection, as Pie.jsx does, so the footer never keeps an empty
      32px gap where the strip would be. */
  }
  {aliados.length > 0 && <FranjaAliados aliados={aliados} idioma={idioma} />}
  <HiloTricolor />
  {
    /* One wrapping flex row at every width. Mobile: contact and stamp share
      the first line (`gap-x-4` = the láminas' 16px) and the annotation is
      pushed onto its own line by `basis-full`, 32px below (`gap-y-8`).
      Desktop: `md:basis-auto` lets it rejoin the row and `order-*` puts the
      stamp first, giving the láminas' stamp | contact | annotation with
      `justify-between`. */
  }
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-8 md:gap-8">
    {
      /* The scan is rendered at 100px below the desktop breakpoint and 120px
        from it up (láminas). `Sello` takes a single `tamano`, so the larger
        value is generated once and sized per breakpoint from the wrapper with
        the direct-child variant — the same "dynamic geometry goes outside the
        canonical component" split FranjaAliados uses for its own heights. */
    }
    <div class="order-2 shrink-0 *:size-25 md:order-1 md:*:size-30">
      <Sello
        imagen={selloCompacto}
        ciudad={selloCiudad}
        fecha={selloFecha}
        tamano={120}
        rotacion={-8}
        idioma={idioma}
      />
    </div>
    <div
      class="order-1 grid min-w-0 flex-1 grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:order-2 md:min-w-55 md:grid-cols-[repeat(2,minmax(160px,auto))] md:gap-x-12"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-etiqueta m-0 font-bold uppercase">
          {t(idioma, 'pie.contacto.email')}
        </p>
        <p class="font-mono text-etiqueta text-tinta-suave m-0 break-words">{email}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-etiqueta m-0 font-bold uppercase">
          {t(idioma, 'pie.contacto.instagram')}
        </p>
        <a
          href={instagram}
          class="font-mono text-etiqueta text-azul-sello inline-flex min-h-11 items-center break-words underline underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:text-azul-marcador active:text-azul-profundo focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-azul-sello"
          >{HANDLE}</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="order-3 basis-full md:basis-auto">
      <Anotacion texto={t(idioma, 'pie.aguante')} rotacion={-2} />
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
